# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Ting Han et al. (2023). Accuracy evaluation of different machine learning force field features.
#   New Journal of Physics. doi:10.1088/1367-2630/acf2bb
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 acdac52d52491b72...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 580 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/han2023.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: linear-regression MLFFs on MTP, SNAP and ACE features
# (registry methods) for amorphous sulfur (300 K, 1500 K, combined) and
# for four carbon phases, fitted with PWmat-MLFF (pacemaker for ACE)
# to total energies, Gaussian-averaged group energies and forces from
# PWmat PBE AIMD; the two exact training RMSEs stated for the combined
# sulfur set. Cosine, Gaussian and simplified DP feature types are
# linear feature models without a registry method and are not encoded
# as runs; most errors are approximate or figure-only.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
